@startuml
title C4 code - Repository intelligence - provider selection
package "Prism MCP server" {
  class "mcp.callRepositoryTool" as Mcp <<existing function>>
  class "ProviderCatalog" as Catalog <<module>>
  class "withRepositoryIntelligence" as Select <<function>>
  class "CompositeRepositoryIntelligence" as Composite <<class>>
  class "NativeRepositoryIntelligence" as Native <<class>>
  class "CodeGraphRepositoryIntelligence" as CodeGraph <<class>>
  class "CodeNibRepositoryIntelligence" as CodeNib <<existing class>>
  class "planRepositoryContext" as Plan <<existing function>>
}

Mcp --> Catalog : lists registered provider availability
Mcp --> Select : requests auto, native, or explicit selection
Select --> Native : always opens the live source authority
Select --> CodeGraph : may add structural evidence
Select --> CodeNib : may add hybrid evidence
Select --> Composite : creates one bounded provider view
Composite --> Native : reads final source ranges
Composite ..> CodeGraph : fuses optional ranked and graph evidence
Composite ..> CodeNib : fuses optional ranked and graph evidence
Mcp --> Plan : creates the public context plan
Plan --> Composite : uses the provider-independent contract

note right of Catalog
  Condition: an external executable or index is unavailable.
  Response: return a sanitized availability record without mutation.
  Governing requirement: repository-intelligence-providers.md section 2.
end note

note right of Select
  Condition: an automatically selected external provider fails.
  Response: retry once with native and record the fallback.
  Governing requirement: repository-intelligence-providers.md section 3.
end note
@enduml
